# L §2.4 Expressions, §2.3 parse rule 3 (tally 2.1.6, issue #81): a [ after a field touches it, whatever the field's
# word: mi.or [k1] prints mi.or[k1], as mi.ks [k2] prints mi.ks[k2]. tally 2.1.5's refcore read or as a keyword
# there and printed mi.or [k1]; the M0 engine too.
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def x: int = mi.or [k1] + mi.ks [k2]
